/* THE HERO SHOT - The Breathalyzer Bypass */
/* Approximate page count: 1.5-2 pages */
/* Power arc: DESPERATE -> TRIUMPHANT */
/* This is the poster image. The Wood Chipper Moment. */

INT. DANNY'S TRUCK - NIGHT

Dashboard glow. The world outside has shrunk to nothing. Only
this matters: Danny, the raccoon, and the machine.

Danny sits behind the wheel. In his lap: the RACCOON. Still
unconscious. Still breathing. Still the worst idea he's ever had.

The BREATHALYZER INTERLOCK DEVICE waits on the steering column.
Red LED. Patient. Unblinking.

Danny lifts the raccoon toward the mouthpiece. Its head lolls.
Its tongue hangs out. It looks dead. It is not dead. Probably.

He holds the raccoon's face near the device.

Nothing happens.

DANNY
Come on.

He adjusts his grip. Tries again. Positions the small snout
directly in front of the mouthpiece.

The raccoon's whiskers twitch. That's it.

DANNY (CONT'D)
Come on, buddy. Breathe for me.

Danny's voice is gentle. Coaxing. The voice you use for a
child, or a dying pet, or a wild animal you've stolen from
a dumpster to commit fraud.

He waits.

The red LED pulses. Waiting for input.

The raccoon does not provide input.

Danny's jaw tightens. He shifts the animal, cradles it like
a baby. Its little arms dangle. Its little face reveals nothing.

DANNY (CONT'D)
Okay. Okay.

He reaches up with one hand. Opens the raccoon's mouth manually.
Tiny teeth. A surprising amount of tiny teeth. He positions
the open mouth toward the device.

Holds.

Waits.

The raccoon's chest rises. Falls. But nothing comes out of
the mouth. Wrong angle. Wrong everything.

Danny pulls back. Stares at the animal. The animal stares at
nothing, because it is unconscious.

DANNY (CONT'D)
(to himself)
Think. Think.

He looks at the raccoon's chest. Watches it rise. Fall. Rise.
Fall. There's air in there. He just needs to get it out.

Danny positions the raccoon again. One hand supporting its
back. The other hand hovering over its belly.

He places his palm on the small chest. Feels the heartbeat
through the fur. Faster than expected. Alive.

DANNY (CONT'D)
Sorry about this.

He squeezes. Gently. Like a bellows. Like CPR for the morally
compromised.

A tiny puff of air escapes the raccoon's mouth.

Danny's eyes go wide.

He repositions. Mouthpiece closer. Much closer.

Squeezes again.

PUFF.

The device BEEPS.

Danny freezes.

CLOSE ON: The IID screen.

Processing...

The moment stretches. The universe holds its breath because
Danny certainly cannot.

GREEN LIGHT.

The LED shifts. Red to green. The most beautiful color Danny
has ever seen.

ENGINE AUTHORIZED appears on the tiny screen.

INT. DANNY'S TRUCK - CONTINUOUS

Danny stares at the green light. At the raccoon. At the green
light again.

DANNY
Holy shit.

Beat.

DANNY (CONT'D)
(louder, wonder breaking through)
Holy shit it worked.

He laughs. The sound is wrong--too loud, too sharp, the laugh
of a man who cannot believe what he has done and knows he
will have to live with it.

The raccoon twitches in his lap. One paw. Then stillness.

Danny looks down at it. His accomplice. His co-conspirator.
His tiny, unconscious partner in crime.

DANNY (CONT'D)
Okay. Okay, we're good. We're good.

He starts the engine. It RUMBLES to life. A small miracle.

Danny shifts the raccoon off his lap. Places it on the
passenger seat. It slumps against the door. Begins to slide.

Danny catches it.

He looks at the raccoon. At the seat. At the seatbelt.

The math takes a moment. The conclusion is inevitable.

INT. DANNY'S TRUCK - CONTINUOUS

Danny reaches across. Grabs the SEATBELT. Pulls it over the
unconscious raccoon.

CLICK.

The raccoon is now buckled in. Passenger seat. Shoulder strap
across its furry chest. Lap belt somewhere around its belly.
Head lolled to one side. Paws limp.

It looks like a very small, very drunk, very unconscious
person heading home from a party that got out of hand.

THE HERO SHOT:

Wide on the truck cab. Danny behind the wheel, scratches on
his hands, sweat on his brow. The unconscious raccoon buckled
into the passenger seat like a tiny, furry designated driver
who has failed at its one job.

The green light of the IID glows on the dashboard. Reflected
in Danny's eyes. In the windshield. In the future that should
not exist but somehow does.

Danny looks at the raccoon. The raccoon does not look back.

DANNY
It's fine.
(beat)
This is fine.

He says it differently this time. Not panic. Not denial.
Relief. Pure, unearned, impossible relief.

Danny puts the truck in gear.

He drives.

The raccoon rides shotgun into the night.

FADE TO:

/* End scene - approximately 2 pages */
/* Note: The seatbelt moment is the Wood Chipper - absurdist visual comedy */
/* The green light is the hero shot - THE poster image for the film */
/* "This is fine" lands different here - it's become a refrain */
